				<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><strong>Madonna</strong>&#8216;s <strong>Rebel Heart</strong> enters the UK album chart at <strong>#2 </strong>with <strong>37,245 </strong>sales, including 416 from streams. This is her 16th Top 2 album.</p>
<p><strong>Rebel Heart</strong> will lengthen <strong>Madonna</strong>&#8216;s lead over her rivals as this <strong>century biggest selling female artist</strong>. Prior to the release of Rebel Heart, <strong>her 792 week 21st century total sale of 7,653,480 (including 86,788 Evita sales) was enough for her to top the list</strong> ahead of Pink (7,377,310), Rihanna (7,084,988) and Adele (6,979,902).</p>
<p><strong>Rebel Heart</strong> is <strong>#1</strong> on the Download Chart, <strong>#3</strong> on the Physical Album chart but only <strong>#33</strong> on the Streaming Album chart.</p>
<p>Good news for <strong>Celebration</strong> that rises 11 places to <strong>#27</strong> in its 99th week!</p>
<p>The post <a rel="nofollow" href="http://drownedmadonna.com/madonnas-rebel-heart-enters-the-uk-albums-chart-at-2/20150315">Madonna&#8217;s Rebel Heart enters the UK Albums Chart at #2.</a> appeared first on <a rel="nofollow" href="http://drownedmadonna.com">Madonna news new album Rebel Heart</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
